        "Content": "New ‘A’ Rated 3 Bedroom House in an exclusive development. Eligible for ‘Help to Buy Scheme & ‘First Home Scheme’\r\n\r\nThis immaculately presented residence is in showhouse condition and extends to 100 sq. m (1,076 sq. ft). It is very conveniently located within walking distance to Bantry Town centre and near beautiful amenities such as Sheeps Head Peninsula, Whiddy Island and Gougane Barra National Park . It is wonderfully situated with a south facing garden and communal green area opposite.\r\n\r\nThe property itself is two storey and it has been architecturally designed to maximise light. The ground floor layout provides for modern comfortable living with an open plan kitchen/dining/living room that opens out onto the rear garden, a laundry, a large wc and understairs storage area. Upstairs there are 2 large double bedrooms, a  single bedroom and a family bathroom. There is access to a large attic space via a Stira.\r\n\r\nThe property benefits from high quality fixtures, fittings and building materials throughout including a fitted kitchen and high quality laminate flooring.\r\n\r\nNo. 7 has two designated car parking spaces and a side access for bins, bikes etc.\r\n\r\nThe property enjoys an excellent position within Bantry. It is approximately 900 metres from the N71, providing direct access east towards Cork and west towards Kenmare, as well as onward routes to surrounding West Cork towns such as Skibbereen, Bandon and Clonakilty.\r\n\r\nCork City and Cork Airport are reachable in approximately 1 hour 20 minutes. Regular bus services also link Bantry with Cork and other regional hubs.\r\n\r\nBantry itself offers a comprehensive range of amenities including leisure facilities, healthcare services, supermarkets, cafés, restaurants, traditional pubs, churches, hotels, and a vibrant selection of local family-run businesses. The town is well served for education with preschools, primary schools, and a respected secondary school all located nearby.\r\n\r\nIn addition to its excellent services, Bantry is surrounded by some of West Cork’s most beautiful natural attractions. Scenic destinations are only a short drive away, offering superb walking routes, beaches, gardens, and panoramic coastal views.\r\n\r\nThis combination of connectivity, amenities, and natural beauty makes Bantry an exceptional place to live.\r\n\r\nFeatures–\r\n\r\nAir to Water Heating System\r\n\r\nHighly Insulated House\r\n\r\nMains Water & Drainage\r\n\r\nOutdoor Tap\r\n\r\nGreen Mortgage Interest Rates are Available for this Home\r\n\r\nEligible for ‘Help to Buy Scheme & ‘First Home Scheme’\r\n\r\nEircode: P75 TK35 (Property Specific Code)\r\n\r\nViewing Is Highly Recommended – By Appointment Only\r\n\r\nDisclaimer: All information provided is to the best of our knowledge but is not guaranteed and should be independently verified. No warranties or representations are made regarding the accuracy, completeness, condition or planning status of the property. Interested parties should satisfy themselves as to the correctness of all information provided, including measurements, boundaries, size or acreage, BER details and services. All measurements and distances are approximate and for guidance only. Photographs and video are for illustrative purposes and may include items not included in the sale (e.g. furniture)."
